{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And if these three.</b> Rashi explained: designation for him [the master] or for his son, and she does not have the means to redeem herself. But one should not explain 'and if these three' as referring to she'er, kesut, and onah — 'he shall not withhold, and she shall go out for nothing, without money' — because that would imply that even if he designated her and did not fulfill these things, she goes out by the signs [of puberty]. And it is obvious that since he designated her, she does not go out except by a get, for she is a full wife." "<b>And she shall go out for nothing.</b> These are the days of na'arut." "<b>Without money.</b> These are the days of bagrut. And both are needed, for if only one verse were written we would establish it for bagrut, which is more straightforward, and if you ask: if she goes out during na'arut, what does she need [this] for during bagrut? — and in the first chapter of Kiddushin it is concluded that it is needed only for a bogeret who is an ailonit, who has no signs of na'arut, who goes out during the days of bagrut."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:39.963395248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}